{"name":"Golf Blazer","hex":"#53a391","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"golf","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Golf of the ICAO/NATO radiotelephony alphabet."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A ball game played by individuals competing against one another in which the object is to hit a ball into each of a series of (usually 18 or nine) holes in the minimum number of strokes.","Alternative letter-case form of Golf from the NATO/ICAO Phonetic Alphabet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/golf"},{"term":"blazer","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A thing which blazes or shines brightly.\n A very bright or hot day.\n\n A dish used to cook directly over the coals of a brazier, or the flame of a chafing dish lamp.\n\n A flat metal piece placed against a fire grate to cause the fire to blaze by creating a draught; a blower.\n\n A comet.","A very bright or hot day."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One who blazes (“announces or proclaims something publicly”); an announcer, a herald, a proclaimer."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blazer"}],"entries":[{"title":"Golf","blocks":[{"text":"Golf is a club-and-ball sport in which players use various clubs to hit a ball into a series of holes on a course in as few strokes as possible. The game was first played in the 15th century in Scotland, and as such, the country is often accredited as \"the home of Golf\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Golfer_swing.jpg/330px-Golfer_swing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golf","wikidata":"Q5377"},{"title":"Blazer","blocks":[{"text":"A blazer is a distinct type of lightweight sports jacket, traditionally made of navy or striped wool or linen. It is typically characterised by metal buttons on the front and sleeves. In terms of formality within Western dress codes, a blazer has a dressier appearance than other sports jackets, yet is seen as less formal than a suit jacket."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Blazer.JPG/330px-Blazer.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blazer","wikidata":"Q883234"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Ming_Emperor_Xuande_playing_Golf.jpg/500px-Ming_Emperor_Xuande_playing_Golf.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Ming_Emperor_Xuande_playing_Golf.jpg/500px-Ming_Emperor_Xuande_playing_Golf.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Xuande Emperor of the Ming dynasty playing chuiwan","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMing_Emperor_Xuande_playing_Golf.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Gloucester%2C_east_window_detail_%2830235780940%29.jpg/500px-Gloucester%2C_east_window_detail_%2830235780940%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Gloucester%2C_east_window_detail_%2830235780940%29.jpg/1280px-Gloucester%2C_east_window_detail_%2830235780940%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Gloucester%2C_east_window_detail_%2830235780940%29.jpg/500px-Gloucester%2C_east_window_detail_%2830235780940%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Stained Glass Window installed in Gloucester Cathedral in the 1350s. Said to be the oldest depiction of the sport.[10]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGloucester%2C_east_window_detail_(30235780940).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Golf_course_Golfplatz